::ALG1_U02_L05_Q01::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q01<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve d = rt for r. {
=A. r = d/t #Correct. Divide both sides by t.
~B. r = d - t #Subtraction does not undo multiplication by t.
~C. r = dt #This does not isolate r.
~D. r = t/d #The quotient is reversed.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q02::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q02<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve y = mx + b for b. {
~A. b = y + mx #The mx term must be subtracted.
~B. b = mx - y #This reverses the subtraction order.
=C. b = y - mx #Correct. Subtract mx from both sides.
~D. b = y/m - x #This solves for a different variable path.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q03::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q03<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve A = bh for b. {
~A. b = A - h #Subtraction does not undo multiplication.
=B. b = A/h #Correct. Divide both sides by h.
~C. b = h/A #The quotient is reversed.
~D. b = Ah #Multiplication does not isolate b.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q04::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q04<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve P = 2l + 2w for w. {
~A. w = P - 2l #This does not divide by 2.
~B. w = P/2 + l #The 2l term must be subtracted first.
~C. w = (P + 2l)/2 #The 2l term should be subtracted.
=D. w = (P - 2l)/2 #Correct. Subtract 2l, then divide by 2.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q05::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q05<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve C = 2pi r for r. {
=A. r = C/(2pi) #Correct. Divide by 2pi.
~B. r = C - 2pi #Subtraction does not undo multiplication by 2pi.
~C. r = 2pi/C #The quotient is reversed.
~D. r = 2pi C #Multiplication does not isolate r.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q06::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q06<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve F = ma for a. {
~A. a = F - m #Subtraction does not undo multiplication by m.
=B. a = F/m #Correct. Divide both sides by m.
~C. a = m/F #The quotient is reversed.
~D. a = Fm #This does not isolate a.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q07::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q07<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve I = Prt for t. {
~A. t = I - Pr #Subtraction does not undo multiplication by Pr.
~B. t = Pr/I #The quotient is reversed.
~C. t = IPr #Multiplication does not isolate t.
=D. t = I/(Pr) #Correct. Divide both sides by Pr.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q08::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q08<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve y = mx + b for x. {
~A. x = y/m + b #The b term must be subtracted before division.
~B. x = (y + b)/m #The b term should be subtracted.
~C. x = m/(y - b) #The quotient is reversed.
=D. x = (y - b)/m #Correct. Subtract b, then divide by m.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q09::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q09<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve V = lwh for h. {
=A. h = V/(lw) #Correct. Divide by lw.
~B. h = V - lw #Subtraction does not undo multiplication.
~C. h = lw/V #The quotient is reversed.
~D. h = Vlw #This does not isolate h.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q10::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q10<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve A = (1/2)bh for h. {
~A. h = A/(2b) #This divides by 2 instead of undoing the one-half.
~B. h = A - (1/2)b #Subtraction does not undo multiplication.
~C. h = b/(2A) #The quotient is reversed.
=D. h = 2A/b #Correct. Multiply by 2, then divide by b.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q11::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q11<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve E = mc^2 for m. {
~A. m = E - c^2 #Subtraction does not undo multiplication by c^2.
=B. m = E/c^2 #Correct. Divide by c^2.
~C. m = c^2/E #The quotient is reversed.
~D. m = Ec^2 #Multiplication does not isolate m.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q12::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q12<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve q = p + r for p. {
~A. p = q + r #The r term must be subtracted.
~B. p = r - q #This reverses the subtraction order.
=C. p = q - r #Correct. Subtract r from both sides.
~D. p = q/r #The operation is addition, not multiplication.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q13::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q13<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve S = 2pi rh for h. {
=A. h = S/(2pi r) #Correct. Divide by 2pi r.
~B. h = S - 2pi r #Subtraction does not undo multiplication.
~C. h = 2pi r/S #The quotient is reversed.
~D. h = 2pi rS #This does not isolate h.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q14::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q14<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve M = 3x + n for n. {
~A. n = M + 3x #The 3x term must be subtracted.
~B. n = 3x - M #This reverses the subtraction order.
=C. n = M - 3x #Correct. Subtract 3x from both sides.
~D. n = M/3 - x #Dividing by 3 is not needed to isolate n.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q15::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q15<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve a = b + cd for d. {
~A. d = a - b - c #The c is multiplied by d and must divide after subtracting b.
~B. d = c/(a - b) #The quotient is reversed.
~C. d = (a + b)/c #The b term should be subtracted.
=D. d = (a - b)/c #Correct. Subtract b, then divide by c.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q16::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q16<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve T = 2x + 5 for x. {
~A. x = T - 5 #This does not divide by 2.
=B. x = (T - 5)/2 #Correct. Subtract 5, then divide by 2.
~C. x = T/2 - 5 #Subtract 5 before dividing by 2.
~D. x = (T + 5)/2 #The 5 should be subtracted.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q17::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q17<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve R = a - b for a. {
=A. a = R + b #Correct. Add b to both sides.
~B. a = R - b #This does not undo subtracting b.
~C. a = b - R #This reverses the relationship.
~D. a = R/b #The operation is subtraction, not multiplication.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q18::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q18<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve N = k/p for k. {
~A. k = N/p #This divides by p instead of multiplying by p.
=B. k = Np #Correct. Multiply both sides by p.
~C. k = p/N #The relationship is reversed.
~D. k = N - p #Subtraction does not undo division by p.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q19::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q19<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve x = (y - z)/w for y. {
~A. y = x/w + z #Multiply by w before adding z.
~B. y = xw - z #After multiplying by w, add z.
=C. y = xw + z #Correct. Multiply by w, then add z.
~D. y = z - xw #This reverses the addition step.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q20::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q20<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve G = h/j + k for h. {
~A. h = (G + k)j #The k term should be subtracted.
~B. h = G - k/j #The subtraction must happen before multiplying by j.
=C. h = j(G - k) #Correct. Subtract k, then multiply by j.
~D. h = (G - k)/j #This divides by j instead of multiplying.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q21::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q21<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Which first step is best when solving y = mx + b for x? {
=A. Subtract b from both sides. #Correct. Remove the added term before dividing by m.
~B. Divide both sides by b. #b is added, not multiplied by x.
~C. Add mx to both sides. #This does not isolate the x-term.
~D. Multiply both sides by m. #The x-term is already multiplied by m.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q22::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q22<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Which formula is equivalent to P = 2l + 2w solved for l? {
~A. l = P - 2w #This does not divide by 2.
~B. l = P/2 - 2w #Only the whole remaining expression should be divided by 2.
=C. l = (P - 2w)/2 #Correct. Subtract 2w and divide by 2.
~D. l = (P + 2w)/2 #The 2w term should be subtracted.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q23::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q23<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>A student solves A = bh for h and writes h = A - b. What is the mistake? {
~A. The student divided when they should have subtracted. #The student subtracted, not divided.
=B. The student subtracted b instead of dividing by b. #Correct. b is multiplied by h.
~C. The student used the wrong target variable only. #The target variable h is correct.
~D. There is no mistake. #The correct formula is h = A/b.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q24::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q24<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Solve K = 4m - n for m. {
~A. m = K + n #This does not divide by 4.
~B. m = (K - n)/4 #The n term should be added to both sides.
~C. m = 4/(K + n) #The quotient is reversed and incorrect.
=D. m = (K + n)/4 #Correct. Add n, then divide by 4.
}

::ALG1_U02_L05_Q25::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L05_Q25<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A1.FND.5<br><br>Question:<br>Why can a formula be rearranged for different variables? {
=A. Equivalent operations preserve the relationship among the quantities. #Correct. The relationship stays true when legal operations are used.
~B. Variables can be replaced by any operation. #Operations must preserve equivalence.
~C. Rearranging removes the need to check work. #Checking is still useful.
~D. A formula has only one possible target variable. #Many formulas can be solved for different variables.
}
